.idea
# Claude Code / agent settings - ALL of it stays local. A committed settings.json
# ships one machine's accumulated permission grants (and its absolute paths) to
# every fork, where they would be pre-approved for someone else's agent.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__
.pytest_cache/
**.egg-info
**/build
**/data
**/quam_state
state_lib/
assets
# No repo-local venv belongs here - the tests run in the shared .venv-qm (ENVIRONMENTS.md).
.venv*
**/calibration_data
/.img
tempCodeRunnerFile.python
temp/

# The Octave mixer-calibration database. quam writes it into the CURRENT WORKING
# DIRECTORY whenever octaves.<name>.calibration_db_path is unset (the case
# quam_fields.octave_calibration_warnings names), so running anything from the
# repo root drops one here. It is a machine artifact, never repo content - one
# was committed for years before the qualibrate removal noticed.
calibration_db.json
**/quam_state_6q
# The OPX+/Octave tree is BUILT, not stored: scripts/make_opxp_fixture.py
# is the tracked artifact, and the tests build into a tmp dir so a fresh
# clone needs no local state at all.
**/quam_state_opxp
